    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0535" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg431"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/899.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 27, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Commander of the <hi rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> telegraphs me that
                    the rebel leaders accede fully to the amended conditions and have so informed
                    the Dominican Government, which is highly gratified at the success of our
                    efforts. The negotiations were closed before the receipt of your telegram
                    concerning, military commanders.</p>
                <p>I believe that the Dominican people are realizing that your policy of assuming
                    that revolutions are no more than a means of securing political power, and that
                    your policy has in this instance saved much human life.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
